{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-analyzer-003-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/Analyzer/InvariantRegistryTests.cs", "line": 137, "method": "CorePurity_AllRules_RunOverInMemoryModel_WithoutFileAccess", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Analyzer/Rules/Inv9RewindPoint.cs:130; that File.Exists call already executes under this test and it stays green -> only an unhandled exception reds it", "what_it_asserts": "InvariantEvaluator.Evaluate over InvariantRegistry.AllRules with an in-memory model throws nothing.", "why_weak": "The name and comment claim the rule core performs no file access, but the only assertion is Record.Exception == null. Inv9RewindPoint (File.Exists/Directory.GetFiles), Inv7bAnnotationStale (Directory.Exists/GetFiles) and Inv10CodecRoundtrip (temp-file write) already touch the filesystem; they merely no-op on a model with a null SaveDirectory. A future rule that reads a real file and succeeds also passes.", "proposed_action": "Either rename to CorePurity_AllRules_DoNotThrow_OverInMemoryModel, or make the claim mechanical: run the sweep with a model whose SaveDirectory points at a guarded sentinel path and assert no probe reached it (or add an AST/source gate over Analyzer/Rules for unguarded System.IO calls).", "effort": "M", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-analyzer-003-02", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/Analyzer/RecordingSectionDump.cs", "line": 59, "method": "Manual_DumpRecordingSections", "category": "T6", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: sut=test-infrastructure; PARSEK_DUMP_SAVE unset returns at RecordingSectionDump.cs:63 before any assertion -> always green", "what_it_asserts": "Nothing. It is an env-gated triage dump that early-returns in CI and has no Assert at all.", "why_weak": "A [Fact] with zero assertions reports as a passing test on every run and inflates the suite tally; its failure modes (a dump that throws) only appear when an operator sets the env var.", "proposed_action": "Keep the tool but stop it counting as a test: gate it with Skip (a SkippableFact / Assert.Skip equivalent) or move the body into a non-[Fact] helper invoked by an explicitly-run entry point, so the suite count reflects real assertions.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
